  "Reduce": {
    "name": "Reduce",
    "kind": "converter",
    "signature": "Reduce(source, seed, accumulator)",
    "summary": "The `Reduce` converter folds `source` into a single value, starting from `seed` and applying `accumulator` to each element.",
    "details": "`source` is a path expression or another getter that resolves to a slice or map.\n\n`seed` is the initial accumulator value.\n\n`accumulator` is a lambda expression with exactly three parameters. The first parameter is the current accumulator value. The second parameter is the element index when reducing a slice (`int64`), or the element key when reducing a map (`string`). The third parameter is the element value. Use `_` as a parameter name to ignore unused parameters.\n\nAn empty slice or map returns `seed` unchanged.\n\nFor maps, element processing order follows map iteration and is not guaranteed to be stable. This matters when `accumulator` is not commutative.",
    "examples": [
      "Reduce(log.attributes[\"counts\"], 0, (acc, _, v) => acc + Int(v))",
      "Reduce(log.attributes[\"labels\"], \"\", (acc, k, v) => Concat([acc, k, \"=\", String(v), \";\"], \"\"))",
      "set(log.attributes[\"total\"], Reduce(log.attributes[\"counts\"], 0, (acc, _, v) => acc + Int(v)))"
    ],
    "anchor": "reduce",
    "featureGate": "ottl.functions.enableLambda"
  },
