  "Substring": {
    "name": "Substring",
    "kind": "converter",
    "signature": "Substring(target, start, length, Optional[utf8_safe])",
    "summary": "The `Substring` Converter returns a substring from the given start index to the specified length.",
    "details": "`target` is a string. `start` and `length` are byte offsets as `int64`. `utf8_safe` is an optional boolean (default: `false`); when `true`, a mid-character `start` advances to the next UTF-8 boundary and a mid-character end (`start+length`) backs up to the previous one, so multi-byte characters are never split, and the result may be shorter than `length` bytes.\n\nIf `target` is not a string or is nil, an error is returned. If the start/length exceed the length of the `target` string, an error is returned.",
    "examples": [
      "Substring(\"123456789\", 0, 3)",
      "Substring(\"一二三\", 0, 4, true)"
    ],
    "anchor": "substring"
  },
  "Time": {
    "name": "Time",
    "kind": "converter",
    "signature": "Time(target, format, Optional[location], Optional[locale])",
    "summary": "The `Time` Converter takes a string representation of a time and converts it to a Golang `time.Time`.",
    "details": "`target` is a string. `format` is a string, `location` is an optional string, `locale` is an optional string.\n\nIf either `target` or `format` are nil, an error is returned. The parser used is the parser at [internal/coreinternal/parser](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector-contrib/tree/main/internal/coreinternal/timeutils). If the `target` and `format` do not follow the parsing rules used by this parser, an error is returned.\n\n`format` denotes a textual representation of the time value formatted according to ctime-like format string. It follows [standard Go Layout formatting](https://pkg.go.dev/time#pkg-constants) with few additional substitutes:",
    "examples": [
      "Time(\"02/04/2023\", \"%m/%d/%Y\")",
      "Time(\"Feb 15, 2023\", \"%b %d, %Y\")",
      "Time(\"2023-05-26 12:34:56 HST\", \"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S %Z\")"
    ],
    "anchor": "time"
  },
